-- title:
--   Proof of Lemma 2.5, p. 12 — given $H_T$, $(Z-\widehat Z_T)'S^k_T \sim N(0,\Theta)$, so $\Pr\{\Gamma\ge\eta\Theta\mid H_T\}=2(1-\Phi(\sqrt\eta))$
-- statement:
--   Work in the model of Section 2 (arms on the unit sphere of $\mathbb R^r$, $r\ge 2$, prior $Z\sim N(0,I_r/r)$, i.i.d. standard normal noise, a fixed deterministic policy $\psi$), with $\widehat Z_T=\mathbb E[Z\mid H_T]$ and vectors $S^1_T,\dots,S^{r-1}_T$ as in Lemma 2.2 (orthonormal, orthogonal to $\widehat Z_T$, measurable functions of $H_T$). Fix $k$ and put
--   $$\Gamma=\Big\{\big(Z-\widehat Z_T\big)'S^k_T\Big\}^2,\qquad \Theta=\mathbb E\big[\Gamma\mid H_T\big].$$
--
--   **Claim (proof of Lemma 2.5, p. 12).** Conditioned on $H_T$, $(Z-\widehat Z_T)'S^k_T$ is normally distributed with mean zero and variance $\Theta$. Consequently, for every $\eta\ge 0$, with probability one,
--   $$\Pr\big\{\Gamma\ge\eta\,\Theta\ \big|\ H_T\big\}\;=\;2\big(1-\Phi(\sqrt\eta)\big),$$
--   where $\Phi$ is the standard normal distribution function.
--
--   This is the step of the paper's proof of Lemma 2.5 that uses the Gaussian posterior: given the history, $Z$ is Gaussian (the prior is Gaussian and the observations are linear in $Z$ with Gaussian noise, the design being a deterministic function of past observations), so its projection on the history-measurable unit vector $S^k_T$, centred at its conditional mean, is a centred normal with variance $\Theta$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The conditional probability is Mathlib's conditional expectation of the indicator of $\{\eta\Theta\le\Gamma\}$ with respect to the σ-algebra generated by $H_T$ under the joint law of $(Z,\eta)$; $\Theta$ is likewise Mathlib's conditional expectation. $\Phi(x)$ is `cdf (gaussianReal 0 1) x`. The identity holds almost surely, which does not depend on the versions chosen. The standing assumptions of Lemma 2.2 are kept as hypotheses for uniformity with Lemmas 2.2, 2.3 and 2.5 (orthonormality guarantees $S^k_T\neq 0$, which is needed; $\eta\ge0$ is needed for $\sqrt\eta$ to be meaningful).
-- source:
--   Rusmevichientong, Tsitsiklis, Linearly Parameterized Bandits, arXiv:0812.3465v2, proof of Lemma 2.5, p. 12 (display defining Pr{Γ ≥ ηΘ | H_T} = 2(1 − Φ(√η)))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LinParamBandits_LowerBound_Model

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace LinParamBandits.LowerBound

/-- Proof of Lemma 2.5, Rusmevichientong, Tsitsiklis, arXiv:0812.3465v2, p. 12: conditioned on
`H_T`, `(Z − Ẑ_T)′ S^k_T` is normal with mean zero and variance `Θ = E[Γ | H_T]`, where
`Γ = ((Z − Ẑ_T)′ S^k_T)²`; hence `Pr{Γ ≥ η Θ | H_T} = 2 (1 − Φ(√η))` almost surely.
Standing assumptions of Sec. 2 (p. 9) as in Lemma 2.2. -/
theorem posterior_direction_tail (r : ℕ) (hr : 2 ≤ r) (ψ : SpherePolicy r) (T : ℕ) (hT : 1 ≤ T)
    (S : Fin (r - 1) → History r T → Vec r)
    (hS_meas : ∀ k, Measurable (S k))
    (hS_orth : ∀ h, Orthonormal ℝ (fun k => S k h))
    (hS_perp : ∀ᵐ ω ∂(P r), ∀ k, inner ℝ (S k (hist ψ ω.1 ω.2 T)) (zhat ψ T ω) = 0)
    (k : Fin (r - 1)) (η : ℝ) (hη : 0 ≤ η) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂(P r),
      ((P r)[{ω' : Ω r | η * ((P r)[fun ω'' : Ω r =>
              (inner ℝ (ω''.1 - zhat ψ T ω'') (S k (hist ψ ω''.1 ω''.2 T))) ^ 2 | histSigma ψ T]) ω'
            ≤ (inner ℝ (ω'.1 - zhat ψ T ω') (S k (hist ψ ω'.1 ω'.2 T))) ^ 2}.indicator
          (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) | histSigma ψ T]) ω
        = 2 * (1 - cdf (gaussianReal 0 1) (Real.sqrt η)) := by sorry

end LinParamBandits.LowerBound
